---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { brandName } from '../lib/site';
import content from '../lib/content';

const { entity, consultant, contactEmail, privacyUpdated } = content.legal;
---

<Legal
  title={`Privacy policy - ${brandName}`}
  description={`How ${brandName} collects, uses, and protects your personal data, in compliance with the GDPR.`}
  path="/privacy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  updated={privacyUpdated}
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal data <strong>{brandName}</strong>, a service operated by
    <strong>{entity}</strong> ("we", "us"), collects, why we collect it, and the rights you have
    over it. It is written to comply with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (the <strong>GDPR</strong>)
    and applicable national data-protection law.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <p>
    The data controller is <strong>{entity}</strong>, represented by {consultant}. For any
    question about this policy or your data, contact us at
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we collect and why</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Data</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
        <th>Legal basis</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Account data: email address, password (stored hashed, never in clear)</td>
        <td>Creating and securing your account, signing you in, sending verification and password-reset emails</td>
        <td>Performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Organization and billing data: organization name, company name, VAT ID, credit balance and transaction history</td>
        <td>Managing your workspace, metering credits, invoicing</td>
        <td>Performance of a contract; legal obligation for accounting records (Art. 6(1)(b) and (c))</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Project data: project descriptions, chat messages, requests, attachments, repository URLs</td>
        <td>Reviewing, estimating, and delivering your project; keeping an auditable history of the engagement</td>
        <td>Performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Project Memory entries, including credentials you choose to share</td>
        <td>Allowing the build agent to complete tasks that need them; entries are encrypted at rest</td>
        <td>Performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Payment data</td>
        <td>Processing credit top-ups and quote payments. Payments are handled by Stripe; we never see or store your card number, only payment references</td>
        <td>Performance of a contract; legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(b) and (c))</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Technical data: IP address, server and proxy logs, essential cookies</td>
        <td>Keeping the platform secure, preventing abuse and fraud, rate limiting, diagnosing incidents</td>
        <td>Legitimate interest in securing the service (Art. 6(1)(f))</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    We collect nothing beyond the table above. In particular, we do <strong>not</strong> use
    third-party analytics, advertising trackers, or marketing databases, we do not send marketing
    emails, and we never sell or rent personal data.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The platform uses <strong>strictly necessary cookies only</strong>: a session cookie to keep
    you signed in and a CSRF token to protect forms. These are exempt from consent under the
    ePrivacy rules, which is why you see no cookie banner. We set no analytics, advertising, or
    cross-site tracking cookies. The signup captcha (Altcha) is self-hosted and sends nothing to
    third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>4. AI processing of your project content</h2>
  <p>
    To deliver an AI-curated build, your project description, chat messages, and relevant Memory
    entries are processed by our AI model provider, acting as a processor on our instructions,
    strictly to review, estimate, and generate your deliverables. This content is not used to
    train models. Builds run in an isolated, sandboxed environment; secrets you store in Memory
    reach only that sandbox, never demo containers or logs.
  </p>
  <p>
    No decision producing legal effects on you is made by automated means alone: every project is
    reviewed by a human ({consultant}) before and during delivery (no processing within the
    meaning of Art. 22 GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>5. Who receives your data</h2>
  <p>Your data is shared only with the processors needed to run the service:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Our hosting provider</strong>, which operates the servers the platform runs on.</li>
    <li><strong>Stripe</strong>, for payment processing (credit top-ups and quotes).</li>
    <li><strong>Our AI model provider</strong>, for the processing described in section 4.</li>
    <li><strong>GitHub or our self-hosted GitLab</strong>, to deliver code: if you connect your own GitHub repository, code and pull requests are pushed there under GitHub's own terms; otherwise delivery happens on our self-hosted GitLab.</li>
    <li><strong>Our email delivery provider</strong>, for transactional emails only (verification, password reset, project status notifications).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Each processor is bound by a data-processing agreement under Art. 28 GDPR. We may also
    disclose data where the law requires it (for example to competent authorities on a valid
    request).
  </p>

  <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    The platform is designed to keep data under European jurisdiction. Where a processor
    transfers data outside the EU/EEA (for example Stripe), the transfer is covered by an adequacy
    decision or the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>7. How long we keep your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account, organization, and project data:</strong> for as long as your account is active, then deleted or anonymized within 90 days of account closure.</li>
    <li><strong>Billing records and invoices:</strong> for the retention period required by applicable accounting law.</li>
    <li><strong>Memory entries and stored credentials:</strong> until you delete them (they are editable and deletable at any time) or your account is closed.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical logs:</strong> up to 12 months.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. How we protect your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All traffic is encrypted in transit (TLS).</li>
    <li>Passwords are stored hashed; sensitive values (credentials, tokens, Memory secrets) are envelope-encrypted at rest.</li>
    <li>AI builds run in isolated, hardened sandboxes; an automated scan blocks any publication that would leak a stored secret.</li>
    <li>Access to production data is restricted to the operator of the service.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If a personal-data breach is likely to result in a risk to your rights, we will notify the
    competent supervisory authority within 72 hours and inform you as required by Art. 33
    and 34 GDPR.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you can, at any time:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you (Art. 15);</li>
    <li><strong>Rectify</strong> inaccurate or incomplete data (Art. 16);</li>
    <li><strong>Erase</strong> your data ("right to be forgotten", Art. 17);</li>
    <li><strong>Restrict</strong> processing (Art. 18);</li>
    <li><strong>Receive</strong> your data in a portable format (Art. 20);</li>
    <li><strong>Object</strong> to processing based on legitimate interest (Art. 21).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, write to
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. We answer within one month. If you
    believe your rights are not respected, you can lodge a complaint with the supervisory
    authority of the country where {entity} is established, or with the supervisory
    authority of your country of residence.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the service evolves. Material changes are announced on the
    platform or by email before they take effect. The date at the top of this page always
    reflects the latest version.
  </p>
</Legal>
